    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8f74e932",
      "@type": "Scene",
      "instance_name": "children_in_cart",
      "label": "Children sitting together in a wooden cart",
      "description": "Two young children, one Black and one white, are seated side-by-side in a wooden cart, both smiling and appearing happy. The Black child is on the left, wearing a patterned hat and a thick coat, while the white child is on the right, wearing a coat with a collar. They are positioned close to each other, suggesting companionship or shared activity. The cart is on a paved surface with playground equipment and trees in the background. The scene is framed by text overlays that imply a racist context.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cd321f98",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_pet",
      "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Black people as property or pets",
      "description": "This stereotype reduces Black individuals to objects of possession or property, implying they are not human beings with inherent dignity but rather commodities to be owned or controlled. The meme explicitly uses the phrase 'new pet' to dehumanize the Black child, framing their presence as something to be owned or enjoyed by the white child, which is a direct and dehumanizing racist trope.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5629afab",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "racism_concept",
      "label": "Concept of Racism",
      "description": "Racism is a system of oppression and prejudice based on race, often involving the belief that one race is inherently superior to others. The meme's text 'when ur too young to know racism' implies that the children are unaware of racial hierarchy, but the image and text together use this ignorance to justify or normalize the racist framing of the Black child as a 'pet'. This requires understanding racism as a social and historical construct, not just a personal attitude.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0735fb63",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "childhood_innocence_as_mask",
      "label": "Use of Childhood Innocence as a Mask for Racism",
      "description": "The meme leverages the perceived innocence of childhood to disguise a racist message. By stating 'when ur too young to know racism', it implies that the children's happiness is pure and uncorrupted, thereby making the racist framing seem more acceptable or less offensive. This requires understanding how societal norms and media often use childhood innocence as a rhetorical device to soften or justify harmful ideologies.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_711af654",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dehumanization",
      "label": "Dehumanization",
      "description": "Dehumanization is the process of stripping away the humanity of a person or group, often to justify mistreatment or exploitation. The meme's use of 'new pet' to describe the Black child is a clear example of dehumanization, reducing a human being to an object. This concept is central to understanding the hateful intent of the meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5ff61815",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "historical_racism",
      "label": "Historical Context of Racial Subjugation",
      "description": "The meme references the historical and ongoing practice of racial subjugation, particularly the commodification of Black people in slavery and other forms of racial oppression. The phrase 'new pet' echoes the historical context of slavery, where Black people were treated as property. Understanding this historical context is necessary to grasp the full weight and hateful nature of the meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_450083be",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "happiness",
      "label": "joyful expression of children",
      "description": "Both children in the wooden cart are smiling broadly, displaying clear signs of happiness and contentment. Their facial expressions convey pure, unadulterated joy, suggesting they are enjoying the moment together.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fd9281c7",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The Black child is mapped as a 'new pet'",
      "description": "The text 'but ur happy cause u got a new pet' explicitly maps the Black child (child1) as an object of possession or property ('new pet'). This is a direct analogical mapping where the textual concept of ownership is projected onto the visual entity of the Black child, reducing their humanity to that of a commodity. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it dehumanizes the child and frames their presence as something to be owned or enjoyed by the white child.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_078133c1",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying ownership of the Black child",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'but ur happy cause u got a new pet', which uses the deictic 'u' (you) to directly address the viewer, making them the one who is happy and owns the 'new pet'. This projection invites the user to identify with the white child's perspective and to internalize the racist framing of the Black child as property. The text 'when ur too young to know racism' also uses 'ur' (you) to address the user, suggesting the user is the one who is too young to understand the racism, thereby projecting the user's innocence onto the scene.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_91a461a6",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme directly attacks Black individuals based on race by dehumanizing the Black child as a 'new pet', reducing their humanity to that of a commodity. This is a clear example of hateful content rooted in racist ideology.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2527f7c6",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who may be exposed to or share racist ideologies, particularly those who are unaware of or indifferent to the historical and ongoing oppression of Black people. The meme is designed to appeal to a community that might find the dehumanizing metaphor of 'new pet' amusing or acceptable, using the guise of childhood innocence to mask its hateful message. It targets those who may not recognize the racist implications or who may be conditioned to view Black people through a lens of objectification and commodification. The meme’s intent is to normalize and trivialize racial subjugation by framing the Black child as a possession rather than a person, thereby appealing to a community that benefits from or is desensitized to such racist tropes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6fd06600"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
  ]
